# 1. Graphical Position Analysis {#sec1}

**Procedure (Week 1 "Steps for position drawing").** For each crank angle θ₂:

a) With centre O, draw OA at θ₂.
b) With centre O, draw OE at θ₁ (fixed) and mark E.
c) With centre A, strike an arc of radius AB. With centre E, strike an arc of radius BE. Their intersection (the one on the same side as in the handout figure) is B.
d) With centre A, draw AC at angle β below AB and mark C (AC = <<n(p.AC*1000,0)>> mm). Join C to B; triangle ABC is link 3.
e) Draw the slider path, a horizontal line H = <<n(p.H*1000,0)>> mm below O.
f) With centre C, strike an arc of radius CD. Its intersection with the slider path (to the right of C) is D.

