# 2. Graphical Velocity Analysis (θ₂ = 60°) {#sec2}

**Known input.** The crank turns about the fixed pivot O, so
$$V_A = \omega_2\,\overline{OA} = <<n(p.omega2,4)>> \times <<n(p.OA,3)>> = <<n(mag(d.VA),3)>>\ \text{m/s},$$
$$\mathbf V_A \perp OA,\ \text{pointing at } \theta_2 + 90^\circ = <<n(ang(d.VA),0)>>^\circ \ (\omega_2\ \text{CCW}).$$

**Relative-motion equations (course steps, Week 3/9 "Help with the Major Assignment").** Underlining shows what is known: two lines = magnitude and direction known, one line = direction only.

$$\begin{aligned}
&\text{Step 1:} && \underset{\perp BE}{\mathbf V_B} = \underset{\perp OA\ (\text{known})}{\mathbf V_A} + \underset{\perp AB}{\mathbf V_{B/A}}\\
&\text{Step 2:} && \mathbf V_C = \mathbf V_A + \underset{\perp AC}{\mathbf V_{C/A}} = \mathbf V_B + \underset{\perp BC}{\mathbf V_{C/B}}\\
&\text{Step 3:} && \underset{\parallel x\text{-}x}{\mathbf V_D} = \mathbf V_C + \underset{\perp CD}{\mathbf V_{D/C}}\\
&\text{Step 4:} && \mathbf V_{G3} = \mathbf V_A + \underset{\perp AG_3}{\mathbf V_{G3/A}} = \mathbf V_B + \underset{\perp BG_3}{\mathbf V_{G3/B}}
\end{aligned}$$

**Construction (scale 1 m/s = 20 mm).** From the pole *o* draw *oa* = V_A (<<n(s2.measured["V_A"].length_exact,1)>> mm long, at <<n(ang(d.VA),0)>>°). Through *a* draw a line ⊥AB, and through *o* a line ⊥BE. They meet at *b* (Step 1). Through *a* draw ⊥AC and through *b* draw ⊥BC; they meet at *c* (Step 2), so the triangle *abc* is the velocity image of link 3. Through *o* draw a horizontal line and through *c* a line ⊥CD; they meet at *d* (Step 3). Point *g₃* is the intersection of ⊥AG₃ through *a* and ⊥BG₃ through *b*. Because G₂, G₄ and G₅ are mid-points of OA, EB and CD, the points *g₂*, *g₄*, *g₅* are the mid-points of *oa*, *ob* and *cd*.

