# 3. Graphical Acceleration Analysis (θ₂ = 60°) {#sec3}

**Normal components (calculated first).** α₂ = 0, so $a^t_A = 0$ and $a_A = a^n_A$. The other normal components use the velocities read from the polygon (Table 6) and always point from the point towards the centre of the relative rotation.

| Component | Formula | Value (m/s²) | Direction |
|---|---|---|---|
| $a^n_A$ | $\omega_2^2\,\overline{OA}$ = <<n(p.omega2,3)>>² × <<n(p.OA,3)>> | <<n(s3.normal.A,2)>> | A → O (∥AO) |
