# 8. Shaking Force, Shaking Moment and Balancing {#sec8}

## 8.1 Shaking force and moment at θ₂ = 60° (course template)

The forces of the moving links on the frame are $\mathbf F_{21} = -\mathbf F_{12}$, $\mathbf F_{41} = -\mathbf F_{14}$ and $\mathbf F_{61} = -\mathbf F_{16}$ (Table 19):

| | x (N) | y (N) |
|---|---|---|
| $F_{21}$ (at O) | <<n(s8.at60.F21[0],2)>> | <<n(s8.at60.F21[1],2)>> |
| $F_{41}$ (at E) | <<n(s8.at60.F41[0],2)>> | <<n(s8.at60.F41[1],2)>> |
| $F_{61}$ (at D, along the guide) | <<n(s8.at60.F61[0],2)>> | <<n(s8.at60.F61[1],2)>> |
| **Sum = shaking force $F_s$** | **<<n(s8.at60.Fsx,2)>>** | **<<n(s8.at60.Fsy,2)>>** |

Table: Table 24 – Forces on the frame at θ₂ = 60°.

$$F_s = \sqrt{\textstyle\sum F_x^2 + \sum F_y^2} = \sqrt{<<n(s8.at60.Fsx,1)>>^2 + <<n(s8.at60.Fsy,1)>>^2} = <<n(s8.at60.Fs,1)>>\ \text{N},$$
$$\phi = \tan^{-1}\frac{<<n(s8.at60.Fsy,1)>>}{<<n(s8.at60.Fsx,1)>>} = <<n(s8.at60.Fs_angle,2)>>^\circ .$$
The shaking (reaction) torque is $T_s = T_{21} = -T_{12} = <<n(s8.at60.T21,2)>>$ N·m, and the shaking moment about O is
$$M_s = T_{21} + \mathbf R_E\times\mathbf F_{41} + \mathbf R_D\times\mathbf F_{61} = <<n(s8.at60.T21,2)>> + <<n(s8.at60.RExF41,2)>> + <<n(s8.at60.RDxF61,2)>> = <<n(s8.at60.Ms,2)>>\ \text{N}\cdot\text{m (CCW)}.$$
Check: $\mathbf F_s = -\sum m_i\mathbf a_{Gi}$ and $M_s = -\sum(\mathbf r_{Gi}\times m_i\mathbf a_{Gi} + I_i\alpha_i)$ give the same values. Friction at the slider does not change $\mathbf F_s$ or $M_s$, only how the load is shared between the bearings.

